  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "From a fake grey-white stone slab, Fang Yuan obtains a terrain map centered on heightened land labeled Di Qiu, with swamps and forests around it and a river at the southwest corner. Four lower lines read as clues: light in the soil, shine up to a hundred thousand feet high, swimming in the sky for a hundred li, praising plum fragrant snow. Painting idea Gu etched the image into his memory so the map remains after the slab fades. He treats it as a Gu Master inheritance clue, then sets it aside because he is busy and cannot place Di Qiu from the map alone.",
      "chapters": [
        496
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_painting_idea_gu",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside Imperial Court blessed land, Fang Yuan sees a mound with a huge tunnel-like hole, swamp, sparse trees, and a long southwest river that matches the remembered map, and asks whether this is Di Qiu inheritance ground. He concludes the owner put huge effort into placing it inside Imperial Court blessed land and using a fake grey-white stone slab, so the inheritance should not be weak.",
      "chapters": [
        552
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "site-discovery-and-construction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_wang_ting_blessed_land",
        "loc_imperial_court_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The marked place is catalogued at Di Qiu. He later confirms that the Gu Master who set up Di Qiu inheritance moved the small tower that should stand above Di Qiu and placed the inheritance on that spot. He also calls it a Gu Immortal inheritance he obtained by accident.",
      "chapters": [
        556
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "site-discovery-and-construction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_di_qiu",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the central control room of Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, he concludes the setter broke that small tower, sealed the gap so the building would not repair it, and meant to use the heavenly power that condenses into the building.",
      "chapters": [
        561
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "site-discovery-and-construction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan judges the mysterious Gu Immortal who created Di Qiu inheritance a refinement grandmaster, because the process uses Eighty-Eight True Yang Building’s heavenly power and leaves him as an assistant rather than the sole refiner.",
      "chapters": [
        566
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "site-discovery-and-construction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the four clue steps, he obtains rank seven Calamity Beckoning Gu inside Water Pavilion.",
      "chapters": [
        567
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-prize",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_calamity_beckoning_gu",
        "house_water_pavilion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He later says he deciphered the code, obtained Di Qiu inheritance, and refined calamity beckoning Gu, but also gained Mo Yao’s will in his mind. Even with that Immortal Gu, he ranks the haul poorly because the Gu is unusable and the will is a heavy burden.",
      "chapters": [
        569
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-prize",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_mo_yao",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After he takes the inheritance, Eighty-Eight True Yang Building restores the Di Qiu hole on the sand table and the cave no longer remains.",
      "chapters": [
        575
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "site-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "That sand-table hole is catalogued at Di Qiu inheritance site. Mo Yao’s will states that when her main body entered Eighty-Eight True Yang Building she obtained an inheritance in the true inheritance secluded domain, created that will from it, and left Di Qiu inheritance both to preserve a chance to refine calamity beckoning Gu and as a trap aimed at Spirit Affinity House.",
      "chapters": [
        644
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "site-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_di_qiu_inheritance_site",
        "loc_true_inheritance_secluded_domain",
        "fac_spirit_affinity_house"
      ]
    }
  ],
